5. YOUR FILES AND PRIVACY

5.1. The Software converts files locally on your computer. It does not upload your files and does not send data to SCADtools or to any third party.

5.2. When a conversion fails, the Software writes logs on your computer. The logs may contain file paths, element names, and the versions of Revit, Windows and the Software. The logs remain on your computer and are sent to SCADtools only if you choose to send them.

5.3. If you choose to send logs or files to SCADtools to report a problem, you confirm that you have the right to do so. SCADtools will use them only to reproduce and fix the problem, will not share them with third parties, and will delete the files once the problem is closed. Do not send files that you are not authorized to share.

5.4. You are solely responsible for your files, including keeping the originals and backups. The Software writes converted copies and does not modify the original file.

6. CONVERSION RESULTS

Each Revit version adds features that earlier versions do not support. A converted file may therefore omit, remove or alter data, and the Software may decline to convert some files. You are responsible for reviewing every converted file before relying on it, including its geometry, elements, families, parameters, schedules, annotations and sheets. The Software is not a substitute for professional review of any project documentation.

